      "mergeID": "66cc8c7b7e03f86237fe08f8",
      "mergedPostDetails": "This started since the last update that changed inputs over to use SteamVR Input 2.0. However, the issue affects Desktop mode Steam Input and OSC.\n\nWhen sending analog look values using a controller through Steam Input or via the OSC address `/input/LookHorizontal`, the input has a very large dead-zone (around 50%) enforced by VRChat, which for controllers is not affected by the dead-zone setting within Steam Input. The old setting felt to be around 10%. \n\nThe new setting makes it uncomfortably hard to use VRChat with a controller, as you have to push the right stick more than halfway to start turning, then the range between slow turning and full speed is extremely narrow and hard to control. While I myself do not use a controller primarily for accessibility reasons, I feel that people who did would have much more trouble with this unexpected change.\n\nThis also makes OSC scripts that I use to turn my character in-game practically useless, as they rely on being able to send small values between 0.1 and 0.5 to turn slowly.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Analog Input Deadzones Too Extreme + Not Configurable",
